{"term":"defend","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:875933fe8cfba5a3c6","definition":"To ward off attacks against; to fight to protect; to guard.","example":"Most Zionists hoped for a state of their own, but early in the 20th century, writers like Hillel Solotaroff and Chaim Zhitlowsky, both Yiddish-speaking immigrant intellectuals in New York, imagined another alternative: a federation of self-governing anarchist communes in Palestine that would defend Jewish life without relying on state power.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["beshield","beward","brood","cape for","defend","fend","guard","preserve","protect","safeguard","secure","shelter","shield","ward"],"antonyms":["attack"],"collocations":[],"usage":"ditransitive","register":"ditransitive, transitive","wordFamily":["defendable","defendant","defendee","defender","defending","dexify","misdefend","outdefend","redefend","underdefend"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/defend#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:66e9b035ad2bd0e301","definition":"To support by words or writing; to vindicate, talk in favour of.","example":"Justice Elena Kagan on Thursday defended the code of conduct the Supreme Court created last year, but conceded there needs to be a way to enforce the rules for it to be more effective.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["beshield","beward","brood","cape for","defend","fend","guard","preserve","protect","safeguard","secure","shelter","shield","ward"],"antonyms":["attack"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["defendable","defendant","defendee","defender","defending","dexify","misdefend","outdefend","redefend","underdefend"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/defend#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9fcacae8cc0c9ad54f","definition":"To make legal defence of; to represen